# The fixes of step 25's review, the terminal layer: findings 10 and 11,
# and the emergency restore's mouse-off under the keyboard protocol and the
# win32 input mode. Record: docs/steps/step-25-fixes/parts/terminal.md.

[break] the-alternate-screen-is-left-with-the-keyboard-flags
rule: The keyboard protocol's flags pushed on the alternate screen are popped before the program leaves it.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::alternate
find: bytes.extend_from_slice(KEYBOARD_OFF);
replace:
caught-by:
    cineris-term terminal::tests::the_keyboard_flags_are_left_pushed_on_neither_screen
    cineris-term terminal::tests::a_resumption_on_the_alternate_screen_pushes_the_flags_on_each_screen_shown

[break] the-alternate-screen-gets-no-keyboard-flags
rule: The keyboard protocol's flags are pushed on the alternate screen once it is shown, while the protocol is on.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::alternate
find: bytes.extend_from_slice(KEYBOARD_ON);
occurrence: 1
replace:
caught-by:
    cineris-term terminal::tests::the_keyboard_flags_are_left_pushed_on_neither_screen

[break] the-main-screen-never-gets-the-flags-of-a-reply-on-the-alternate
rule: Flags pushed while the alternate screen was shown are pushed on the main screen once it is back.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::alternate
find: let push_main = self.keyboard && !self.main_keyboard;
replace: let push_main = false;
caught-by:
    cineris-term terminal::tests::the_keyboard_flags_are_left_pushed_on_neither_screen

[break] a-reply-on-the-alternate-screen-is-taken-as-on-the-main
rule: A push written while the alternate screen is shown is not the main screen's.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::reply
find: self.main_keyboard = !self.alternate;
replace: self.main_keyboard = true;
caught-by:
    cineris-term terminal::tests::the_keyboard_flags_are_left_pushed_on_neither_screen

[break] the-end-leaves-the-alternate-screen-with-the-keyboard-flags
rule: Putting the terminal back pops the alternate screen's flags before it leaves the alternate screen.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::end
find: end.extend_from_slice(KEYBOARD_OFF);
occurrence: 1
replace:
caught-by:
    cineris-term terminal::tests::the_keyboard_flags_are_left_pushed_on_neither_screen

[break] a-resumption-on-the-alternate-screen-counts-the-main-screen-pushed
rule: Continued after a stop on the alternate screen, the flags are pushed on the main screen once it is back.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::resume
find: self.main_keyboard = self.keyboard && !self.alternate;
replace: self.main_keyboard = self.keyboard;
caught-by:
    cineris-term terminal::tests::a_resumption_on_the_alternate_screen_pushes_the_flags_on_each_screen_shown

[break] the-restore-leaves-the-keyboard-flags-on-the-alternate-screen
rule: The emergency restore with the alternate screen and the keyboard protocol on pops the flags before it leaves the alternate screen.
